Z||000000||fiero_se86||08-19-2001||08:59 PM||||im 17 i have a 86 fiero se. it has 77k on it. ive already put a new moter in it clutch, and now i just put in a tranny. is it worth keeping or do they break down alot. if i sell it im going to buy a 1975 chevy monza with over $6,000 in performance parts in it, it is a very very nice car. what do u think i should do.||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||08-19-2001||09:07 PM||||If you put all that stuff into the Fiero alreayd you might as well keep it and keep putting more into it,   Fiero's like it when you put money into them||||reg||1
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||08-19-2001||09:10 PM||||YES keep it... your now past the major problems youll ever have!  If you do burnouts youll be puttin another tranny in it soon!!  I know i have done 5 trannys, 4 engines, 1 4 to 6 swap, a auto to manual swap, brakes, acles, axle seals, wheel bearings, tie rods,wiring harness's, buttons, switches, headlight motors, tires, neons, and a new stereo just to name a FEW of my Fiero experiences and the MORE i do the MORE i love my damn little car!!!  Note that not all the engines and trannies were in my car... the 4 - 6 swap & auto to manual swap was James's 88 coupe... One motor and tranny is claimed to Jesse's 3100 HO Fiero!<P>Yes though keep it... Not much handles close and is as quick... and as for that monza... yea she has 6,000 in parts but when one breaks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> (as ****  frequently does on hi-po motors) your paying a arm and a leg... at LEAST... maybe a hand or two! <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||10
Z||000003||FieroKyle||08-19-2001||10:55 PM||||why do you ask??? its obvious!!! YES!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||08-19-2001||10:59 PM||||I understand the Monza lust. Used to have one with a 350. Lots of fun. Pain in the ass to work on. Everything is shoehorned in. <BR>I would also be asking myself why he's selling something that he's got that much money tied up in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>Having said that... Keep the Fiero! Has really low miles, and as others have mentioned, you've already replaced most of the stuff that breaks. I would guess that Fiero parts will be easier to find, too.<BR>If you find yourself with a bunch of disposable income, you can do some <I>insane</I> motor swaps in a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
